Legally there is nothing to prevent us from going to live in the wild like
primitive people or from going into business for ourselves. But in practice
there is very little wild country left, and there is room in the economy for
only a limited number of small business owners. (Paragraph 73)

Even the small-business owner commonly has only limited autonomy. Apart from
the necessity of government regulation, he is restricted by the fact that he
must fit into the economic system and conform to its requirements. (Paragraph
120)

I was searching for another paragraph in ISAIF, where it was explained how the
average person wanting to get into small business had to get a franchise, and
franchises tended to keep out the kind of person needing autonomy.





